# Highlight overdue outreach contact headers
Workstream-ID: lea-27
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/27
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded hiring-outreach presentation improvement
Status: DONE
Milestone: Identify overdue outreach before opening contact details
Dependencies: lea-26

## Purpose
Highlight the collapsed contact title for the existing overdue outreach group.
Reuse the priority table's strictly-over-seven-day, no-initial-outreach rule;
do not invent an expiration date or change message delivery.

## Tasks
- [x] Inspect the existing priority classifier and native expander/theme APIs.
- [x] Add scoped header emphasis and an explicit overdue text label.
- [x] Preserve regular headers, native interaction and note/undo/completion actions.
- [x] Qualify regression cases and actual fictional browser presentation.
- [x] Update affected guidance and prepare scoped issue/Project/backlink completion.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Every priority contact has a visibly highlighted collapsed title.
- [x] An explicit overdue label conveys urgency without relying on color alone.
- [x] Recent, note-sent and unavailable-date contacts do not receive overdue emphasis.
- [x] Marking/undoing a connection note removes/restores the intended header emphasis.
- [x] Native expansion, focus and explicit completion remain functional.
- [x] Dark/light themes and a narrow viewport retain readable, contained headers.
- [x] Existing classification, editors, application history and prior work remain intact.
- [x] Only fictional state is used; private inputs and independent applications are preserved.
- [x] One repository issue, one issue-backed Project item and a durable backlink represent the workstream.

## Completion evidence
Local technical implementation is complete. Native collapsed titles reuse the
priority contact IDs and show an explicit Overdue outreach label with red text,
tint, border and left accent. Regular titles and message-body styling remain
normal; neither a second age rule nor an expiration deadline is introduced.

The regression fails against the old renderer. All seventeen focused dashboard
cases, Black, Ruff and scoped mypy pass. Six actual fictional browser boundaries
pass with six successful backend completions and no page errors or external
requests. Actual native dark/light configuration, keyboard expansion/focus,
contained 600-pixel titles, note/undo reclassification and per-contact completion
with reload are verified. Application history is retained. The final dark/light
and narrow contact-title captures were directly reviewed.

Five affected guides explain the same membership and explicit priority cue.
Both identified owned fixture processes/listeners are stopped and absent; only
their inspected fictional database and empty root are removed. Prior local
source, twenty-six tracking records and selected private metadata are preserved.
Initial issue/Project/backlink read-back is independently verified. Final scoped
completion settlement belongs in the excluded index/ledger, not a repeatedly
rewritten managed description.

This is local technical completion, not live qualification, human acceptance
or publication. Existing sent-note decoration is unchanged and not newly
qualified. No live outreach, independent runtime control, commit, push or release.

